WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.490
The countdown to Eleven and the gang's big
showdown with Vecna and the Mind Flayer has

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:06.490
begun.

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:10.570
And it looks like the Upside Down's villains
could well win the next battle,

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.509
It is over Eleven.

00:00:12.509 --> 00:00:14.440
You have freed me.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.860
You can't stop this now.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:22.200
with El's failure to beat the big bad foreshadowed
when Dustin rolled an 11 and failed to beat

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.860
Vecna in his D&amp;D game at the start of Season
4.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.420
That's a miss!

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:32.320
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining all the clues to

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:37.370
why Eleven and co will need to use time travel
to eventually defeat the show's villains.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.180
Spoilers and speculation ahead, so take care.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:45.230
The idea of time travel in Stranger Things
was heavily hinted towards the end of Season

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:49.230
3, when Dustin, Erica, Steve and Robin stumbled
into a screening of Back To The Future.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:53.720
Einstein has just become the world's first
time traveler!

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:58.140
And right off the bat in Season 4, in Eleven's
opening scene she says this:

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:01.200
Today is Day 185.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.710
Feels more like ten years.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:04.689
Joyce says time is funny like that.

00:01:04.689 --> 00:01:07.280
Emotions can make it speed up or slow down.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.550
We are all time travellers if you think about
it.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:14.690
The idea that happy or sad feelings can affect
the way we perceive time is analogous to how

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:19.550
Eleven draws on joyful memories, like her
mother's love, to take down One in their first

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:25.250
confrontation, versus how Vecna exploits his
victim's feelings of guilt and sorrow to trap

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.620
them, then kill them.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:32.350
And there are clues right from the pilot episode,
through seasons two and three, then four,

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:37.229
that time and its representation through clock
motifs will be crucial to understanding and

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:39.810
defeating the villains of the Upside Down.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:45.100
For starters, we know that One hated the way
humans use time to impose their own sense

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:49.890
of order on the world, something we see during
his villain's monologue while a young Henry

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:52.840
Creel stares at the Creel House grandfather
clock

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:59.340
Seconds, minutes, hours, days, weeks, months,
years, decades.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:03.580
Each life a faded, lesser copy of the one
before.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:08.479
The way he reverses the hands on the grandfather
clock, not only points to his disdain for

00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:13.640
the norms of how time usually works, but it's
also a little clue to time reversal and travel

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:14.999
in the show.

00:02:14.999 --> 00:02:18.489
And given the Alice in Wonderland reference
via his sister's name,

00:02:18.489 --> 00:02:20.439
It looks like a fairy tale.

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:24.909
when the young Henry kills a rabbit, it's
not surprising as it's like he's killing the

00:02:24.909 --> 00:02:29.299
character who was obsessed with time in the
Lewis Carroll story.

00:02:29.299 --> 00:02:34.109
It's also curious how all the way back in
the first season, when Eleven makes her first

00:02:34.109 --> 00:02:39.459
contact with the Demogorgon, the event that
rips open a gate to the Upside Down in Hawkins,

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:44.349
there's the sound of a clock ticking while
she's in the Void, hinting at Vecna's presence

00:02:44.349 --> 00:02:49.950
in the background.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:55.690
There's also a chiming sound effect in Season
1's first episode after Will sees the Demogorgon

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:59.819
and falls off his bike.

00:02:59.819 --> 00:03:05.659
Then at the very end of Season 2 episode 4,
after Hopper goes into the Mind Flayer's tunnels,

00:03:05.659 --> 00:03:10.659
you can hear the sound of a clock ringing.

00:03:10.659 --> 00:03:15.549
And in the third season, just after the Mind
Flayer possesses Billy and he gets pulled

00:03:15.549 --> 00:03:20.889
into the Upside Down, there's the sound of
clocks chiming in the background.

00:03:20.889 --> 00:03:26.939
What do you want?

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:32.159
And after Billy comes out of that vision,
you can also hear a gong as he staggers around

00:03:32.159 --> 00:03:40.049
suffering from being in the heat and the sun.

00:03:40.049 --> 00:03:45.239
The Hawkins clocktower also appears in the
first shot of the Horror in the Heartland

00:03:45.239 --> 00:03:50.860
news report in Season 3, which is also another
Back To The Future easter egg given the importance

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:54.229
of the clocktower to time travel in that movie.

00:03:54.229 --> 00:03:58.590
And thanks to two of our amazing movie lovers,
Rebecca Strain and Arianna, for noticing that

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:05.089
Max's counsellor Ms Kelly wears a clock necklace,
which I think also looks rather like a key,

00:04:05.089 --> 00:04:10.949
a possible hint that time will be the answer
to how the gang eventually defeat Vecna.

00:04:10.949 --> 00:04:15.549
Another possibility for this detail is that
it's a hint that Ms Kelly is being used in

00:04:15.549 --> 00:04:20.920
some way by Vecna or the Mind Flayer, similar
to how Will and Billy were spies for the villain.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:26.229
After all, Max discovered the therapist had
been helping Chrissy and Fred, both of whom

00:04:26.229 --> 00:04:28.150
end up as Vecna's victims.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:29.820
Fred was seeing Ms. Kelley too.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:33.780
Another clock-related detail that another
of our awesome movie lovers Chris Vellner

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:39.900
pointed out is how Black Widow spiders often
have hour glass markings on their abdomen,

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:45.090
something you can see when a young Henry Creel
is drawing one, a lethal clue also to how

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:49.790
once Vecna ensnares you, the countdown begins
to your death.

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:55.450
There's also a deep-cut time-related connection
between One and Watchmen, as the same musical

00:04:55.450 --> 00:05:02.250
theme plays when One reveals his origin story
as also plays during the birth of Dr Manhattan.

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:08.450
Like Stranger Things, Watchmen heavily features
clock motifs, and Dr Manhattan also has the

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:11.920
ability to experience time in a non-linear
way.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:18.870
Both the awakening of Henry Creel's powers
and Dr Manhattan's birth take place in 1959,

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:24.840
and on top of that the main events of Season
4 take place in 1986, the same year that the

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:27.570
Watchmen comics were first published.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:32.740
And the way Eleven evaporates One into dust,
sending him into the Upside Down where he

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:37.810
becomes Vecna, has parallels with the way
Jon Osterman is evaporated by accident during

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:42.890
a radioactive particle test and disappears
before becoming Dr Manhattan.

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:49.410
Now, a character a lot of you have been asking
about is Eight, aka Kali, Eleven's lost sister

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.640
who she met back in Season 2.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:55.350
She's mentioned in Season 4 by One when he's
talking to Eleven:

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:58.270
Do you remember the day a strange woman came
to see you?

00:05:58.270 --> 00:05:59.910
This would've been when Eight was still here.

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:04.590
It seems pretty clear then that Eight used
her powers to cast illusions to escape the

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:08.650
lab before One went on his rampage and killed
the other test subjects.

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:14.250
And I think she'll be back before everything
is over to help Eleven take down Vecna and

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:15.250
the Mind Flayer.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:20.420
Or, given her hatred of Brenner and the Hawkins
lab, it's possible she could ally with One

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:21.420
instead.

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:26.070
In fact, there was some foreshadowing of her
return in the crossword that Brenner completes

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.740
in the opening scene.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:32.310
One of the clues is for the "Wife of Shiva",
the answer to which is Kali.

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:37.950
In the Hindu tradition, Kali is the Goddess
of Time, Change and Death, and perhaps together

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:42.120
with Eleven, they will find a way to reverse
an event in time.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:46.460
Also next to the crossword in that newspaper
is another clock-related easter egg with an

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:50.690
ad for a jewellers and watchmakers who offer
"watch repairing" services.

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:56.110
Now, if any of these clues seem too coincidental,
it's worth remembering that the Duffer Brothers

00:06:56.110 --> 00:07:01.370
have said that right from the very beginning
of the series, they wrote a 25-page document

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:06.200
which outlined all the mythology for the show
and the Upside Down and how it worked.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:12.340
Plus, the show's set decorator has said that
'every item, every tiny piece of set dressing,

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:13.700
is intentional.'

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:16.190
So, Dustin's Sherlock Holmes quote...

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:21.520
The world is full of obvious things which
nobody by any chance ever observes.

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:25.840
... is basically telling us that the clues
and answers to the mysteries behind Stranger

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:30.170
Things are all laid out in little details
in the show.

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:35.360
On top of that, before it was renamed Stranger
Things, the original title for the show was

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:36.360
Montauk.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:41.960
Montauk is the name of a real-life place on
Long Island which has inspired numerous conspiracy

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:45.650
theories about experiments carried out at
the military base there.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:50.690
According to Wikipedia, a book called "The
Montauk Project: Experiments in Time" claims

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:55.570
experiments at the government facility opened
"a porthole in time" that "allowed […] travel

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:59.240
[to] anywhere in time or space" via a "time
tunnel".

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:04.020
The book also describes the time an alien
monster travelled through the tunnel, causing

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:07.220
damage and killing numerous people before
it was killed.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:12.639
A lot of evidence then points to time travel
playing some crucial part in Stranger Things

00:08:12.639 --> 00:08:17.400
before the final season is over, and the Duffer
Brothers have said that the first part of

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:23.190
Season 4 is the beginning of the end, so to
quote the Time-manipulating wizard Doctor

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.550
Strange,
We're in the Endgame now.

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:29.560
I think it's possible that Season 4 will end
on a cliffhanger, perhaps a tragedy affecting

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:33.990
one of the main characters that will need
some kind of time travel to fix.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:38.289
This could be similar to Avengers: Infinity
War where the heroes lose, and many of them

00:08:38.289 --> 00:08:43.321
seemingly die, only to eventually return in
Endgame when the Avengers use time travel

00:08:43.321 --> 00:08:44.660
to fix things.

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:49.589
The most extreme outcome could be that all
the show's events are undone so that Eleven

00:08:49.589 --> 00:08:52.889
is never taken from her mother and lives a
normal, happy life.

00:08:52.889 --> 00:08:58.870
I don't think wiping out the entire story
would be especially popular though, so let's

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:01.879
hope whatever is planned is something more
interesting than that.

00:09:01.879 --> 00:09:06.220
Funnily enough, there was a Rick and Morty
easter egg in Season 4, via the name Rick

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:11.209
Sanchez which appears on the list of Ricks
that the gang searches for at the video store.

00:09:11.209 --> 00:09:15.920
Interestingly, Rick and Morty, a show which
features multiple alternate universes, initially

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:21.160
had a no-time-travel rule until it introduced
a whole episode to show why time travel was

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.920
such a bad idea.

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:27.399
Of course, Stranger Things is always loaded
with incredible details, such as the hidden

00:09:27.399 --> 00:09:33.290
sound effect that reveals how as a child Henry
Creel might have got his powers from the Upside

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:36.550
Down, which I explain in my Season 4 easter
eggs video.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.639
Tap here to watch that or follow the link
in the video description.

00:09:39.639 --> 00:09:45.230
So, movie lovers, how do you think time travel
will end up being used in Stranger Things?

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:48.709
Or do you think there's another way to defeat
Vecna and the Mind Flayer?

00:09:48.709 --> 00:09:50.839
Let me know in the comments below.

00:09:50.839 --> 00:09:56.050
Next, tap here for my full breakdown of the
ending of Volume 1 and what else to expect

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:58.079
in the big Part 2 finale.

00:09:58.079 --> 00:10:01.970
And if you liked this video, do leave a thumbs-up,
I really appreciate it.

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:05.939
Thanks for enjoying Stranger Things with me
and hope you have a marvellous movie-loving

00:10:05.939 --> 00:10:06.939
week!

00:10:06.939 --> 00:10:07.880
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

